  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466366",
      "title": "Observing Different Types of Responses",
      "lectureOrder": 595,
      "videoOrder": 548,
      "sourceHash": "d6451f1679c4f23e20bfe4f74b43b5eb646de80591cf6ee581e4081d8f779577",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "Instructor: Thus far, we always were only interested",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 8.82,
          "en": "in the response data of our request, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.82,
          "end": 11.34,
          "en": "For example, when we fetch the posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.34,
          "end": 12.51,
          "en": "we get the response data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.51,
          "end": 14.82,
          "en": "we map that and we return the subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 17.61,
          "en": "and then we use that data in the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.61,
          "end": 20.49,
          "en": "Nothing wrong with that and absolutely what we need here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.49,
          "end": 24.12,
          "en": "but sometimes you need access to the entire response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.12,
          "end": 26.37,
          "en": "and not just to the extracted body data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.37,
          "end": 28.59,
          "en": "Sometimes you need to find out which status code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.59,
          "end": 31.74,
          "en": "was attached, or you need some response headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.74,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "And in such cases, you can change the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 39.48,
          "en": "the Angular http client parses that response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.48,
          "end": 42.45,
          "en": "and you can basically tell Angular, hey,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.45,
          "end": 45.15,
          "en": "please don't give me the unpacked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.15,
          "end": 48.03,
          "en": "the extracted response data you found in the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.03,
          "end": 50.46,
          "en": "give me the full response instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 53.97,
          "en": "And let's do that for sending a post request, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 56.52,
          "en": "You'd do that by adding this extra argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.52,
          "end": 60.03,
          "en": "to configure the request, and here I won't set any headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.03,
          "end": 65.03,
          "en": "or perms, instead here, we can change the observe key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.78,
          "end": 68.94,
          "en": "Observe takes a couple of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.94,
          "end": 71.49,
          "en": "and IntelliSense here incorrectly shows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.49,
          "end": 73.41,
          "en": "that it can only set body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.41,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "That actually is the default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 79.35,
          "en": "and body means that you get that response data extracted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.35,
          "end": 83.01,
          "en": "and converted to a JavaScript object automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.01,
          "end": 85.26,
          "en": "But you don't have to stick to body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.26,
          "end": 88.65,
          "en": "You can for example, also change this to response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.65,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "By the way, you should get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 94.28999999999999,
          "en": "if you enter something incorrect, but response is supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.28999999999999,
          "end": 96.21000000000001,
          "en": "Now let's see what this is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.21000000000001,
          "end": 99.09,
          "en": "We are already logging the response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.09,
          "end": 101.85,
          "en": "or whatever we get back here in the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.85,
          "end": 105.24000000000001,
          "en": "so we should see that when we add a new post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.24000000000001,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "So let's simply enter some content here, doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 109.5,
          "en": "Let's send that post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.5,
          "end": 113.72999999999999,
          "en": "And now you see you get back the full http response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.72999999999999,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "You have the body in there and conveniently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 119.49000000000001,
          "en": "this still already was parsed and converted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.49000000000001,
          "end": 121.47,
          "en": "to a JavaScript object for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.47,
          "end": 123.24,
          "en": "but if you wanted to access it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.24,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "you would now have to access it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "by typing responseData.body here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 129.39,
          "en": "and you even get auto completion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 130.92,
          "en": "because TypeScript understands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.92,
          "end": 133.173,
          "en": "that we request a full response here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 134.19,
          "end": 136.07999999999998,
          "en": "So you still have access to that body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.07999999999998,
          "end": 139.95,
          "en": "but now you also have access to the headers of the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.95,
          "end": 143.97,
          "en": "to the status code, the status text, if it was okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.97,
          "end": 146.16,
          "en": "which will be true if the status code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 149.16,
          "en": "is in the 200 XX region.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 149.16,
          "end": 152.37,
          "en": "So if it's not a 400 or 500 status code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.37,
          "end": 155.55,
          "en": "And that can be more useful in some scenarios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "where you maybe don't care about the body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 160.11,
          "en": "or not only about the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 160.11,
          "end": 163.53,
          "en": "but you actually want more information than just that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 163.53,
          "end": 167.4,
          "en": "With observe, you can change the kind of data you get back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.4,
          "end": 170.16,
          "en": "Now this is how you observe the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.16,
          "end": 174.06,
          "en": "You can also observe something different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.06,
          "end": 177.42000000000002,
          "en": "So here when we delete posts, I will use observe again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.42000000000002,
          "end": 179.73,
          "en": "and I mentioned that body would be the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 179.73,
          "end": 181.89,
          "en": "and that extracts the response body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.89,
          "end": 183.96,
          "en": "and converts it to JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 186.33,
          "en": "You also have response as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 186.33,
          "end": 190.65,
          "en": "Now you also have events. Now what is events?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 190.65,
          "end": 193.95,
          "en": "Let's simply have a look at this events thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 193.95,
          "end": 196.26,
          "en": "by using one hour operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 196.26,
          "end": 198.06,
          "en": "which we can chain in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 198.06,
          "end": 200.49,
          "en": "and we import that from RxJS Operators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 200.49,
          "end": 202.29,
          "en": "and that's the tap operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 202.29,
          "end": 205.05,
          "en": "And that simply allows us to execute some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 205.05,
          "end": 207.51,
          "en": "without altering the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 207.51,
          "end": 211.11,
          "en": "so that we basically just can do something with the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 211.11,
          "end": 213.72,
          "en": "but not disturb our subscribe function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 213.72,
          "end": 217.35,
          "en": "and the functions we passed as arguments to subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 217.35,
          "end": 221.76,
          "en": "So here I simply pipe(tap) in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 221.76,
          "end": 226.76,
          "en": "I get my my event presumably, since we observe events here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 227.13,
          "end": 228.45,
          "en": "and I can console.log this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 228.45,
          "end": 231.66,
          "en": "and you don't need to return anything or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.66,
          "end": 235.5,
          "en": "It won't interrupt the normal observable data flow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 235.5,
          "end": 238.38,
          "en": "It just taps in there, allows you to do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.38,
          "end": 242.16,
          "en": "but then automatically lets the response pass through,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.16,
          "end": 243.63,
          "en": "so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 243.63,
          "end": 245.19,
          "en": "So let's see what that gives us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 245.19,
          "end": 250.19,
          "en": "If I now click clear posts, we see we get two outputs now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 250.8,
          "end": 254.73,
          "en": "and these outputs stem from post service line 70",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.73,
          "end": 257.16,
          "en": "which clearly is this console log.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 257.16,
          "end": 259.98,
          "en": "So it seems like we get two events here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 259.98,
          "end": 262.89,
          "en": "The first one logs an empty object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 262.89,
          "end": 266.88,
          "en": "or an almost empty object, where we have type zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 266.88,
          "end": 270.72,
          "en": "And the second one is the http response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 270.72,
          "end": 273.12,
          "en": "In the end, you have different type of events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 273.12,
          "end": 275.58,
          "en": "and they are encoded with numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 275.58,
          "end": 278.31,
          "en": "However, here in code you don't have to use these numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 278.31,
          "end": 279.903,
          "en": "you have a more convenient way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 281.73,
          "end": 285.48,
          "en": "We can check event type and compare this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 285.48,
          "end": 289.05,
          "en": "to http event type, which is an enum",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 289.05,
          "end": 293.49,
          "en": "you can import from @angular/common/http.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 293.49,
          "end": 296.94,
          "en": "This is supported in TypeScript only, and for JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 296.94,
          "end": 299.19,
          "en": "this is the end just as a map of numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 299.19,
          "end": 300.69,
          "en": "so of zero and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 300.69,
          "end": 302.67,
          "en": "and it understands which type of event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 302.67,
          "end": 303.69,
          "en": "so which number here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 303.69,
          "end": 306.69,
          "en": "stands for which internal type of event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 306.69,
          "end": 308.82,
          "en": "But here we have a more human readable way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 308.82,
          "end": 310.59,
          "en": "because now if you type a dot here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 310.59,
          "end": 312.6,
          "en": "you see the different translations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 312.6,
          "end": 315.27,
          "en": "Now these are just the responses for the numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 315.27,
          "end": 317.97,
          "en": "you see in that log here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 317.97,
          "end": 320.94,
          "en": "And you can actually see that here in the preview.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 320.94,
          "end": 323.01,
          "en": "You see, for example, response has a type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 323.01,
          "end": 324.51,
          "en": "of four by the look of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 324.51,
          "end": 327.24,
          "en": "This is simply number four encoded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 327.24,
          "end": 328.86,
          "en": "in more human readable text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 328.86,
          "end": 330.9,
          "en": "And again, that's a TypeScript only feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 330.9,
          "end": 335.19,
          "en": "It is compiled to just that number comparison in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 335.19,
          "end": 338.79,
          "en": "And you see that, for example, send has that number of zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 338.79,
          "end": 341.31,
          "en": "so it looks like we had the sent event first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 341.31,
          "end": 345.03,
          "en": "and then we had the response event and that was oslo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 345.03,
          "end": 348.3,
          "en": "There are other events too, which didn't kick in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 348.3,
          "end": 350.25,
          "en": "For example, when you were uploading files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 350.25,
          "end": 353.04,
          "en": "you would get back some progress information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 353.04,
          "end": 357.15,
          "en": "about that file upload, how it is going and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 357.15,
          "end": 360.09,
          "en": "So here, if you ever, for example, want to check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 360.09,
          "end": 362.28,
          "en": "yeah, did I get back the response?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 362.28,
          "end": 366.93,
          "en": "Then you can just compare the event type to this event type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 366.93,
          "end": 370.8,
          "en": "so to this number and see are we having the response here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 370.8,
          "end": 373.41,
          "en": "And if you do have the response, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 373.41,
          "end": 377.877,
          "en": "you could log the event body because you know, okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 377.877,
          "end": 381,
          "en": "the event we have here is actually my response object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 381,
          "end": 382.92,
          "en": "I can safely access the body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 382.92,
          "end": 386.46,
          "en": "If you just sent this, so if the type is equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
